@@ -0,0 +1,83 @@
+# USDC Pay
+
+A minimal dApp for sending **USDC on Ethereum mainnet**. Connect a wallet,
+see your USDC and ETH balances, and pay anyone by address.
+
+The whole app is the `/pay` page (`/` redirects there).
+
+## Stack
+
+Production-standard Ethereum frontend stack:
+
+- **Next.js 15** (App Router) + **React 19** + **TypeScript** (strict)
+- **wagmi v2** + **viem v2** — typed contract reads/writes and wallet state
+- **RainbowKit** — wallet connection UI (MetaMask, Coinbase, WalletConnect, …)
+- **TanStack Query** — caching/refetching of on-chain reads (bundled with wagmi)
+
+## How it handles USDC faithfully
+
+USDC is treated as the real mainnet token, not a toy:
+
+- Address `0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48`, checksummed at import
+  time via `getAddress` (`src/lib/usdc.ts`).
+- **6 decimals, not 18.** Every conversion goes through `USDC_DECIMALS`.
+  Amounts are parsed with `parseUnits(value, 6)` and the input rejects more
+  than 6 fractional digits instead of silently rounding a payment.
+- Transfers call the ERC-20 `transfer(to, amount)` on the real contract using
+  viem's standard `erc20Abi` — no hand-rolled ABI.
+
+## Safety / UX guardrails
+
+- Recipient address is validated and checksum-checked; mixed-case typos are
+  rejected, lowercase pastes are normalized.
+- Blocks sending to the zero address or to the USDC contract itself (would
+  burn funds), and warns when paying your own address.
+- Amount is capped to your balance; "Max" fills the exact balance to the wei.
+- Warns when you have **no ETH for gas** and disables sending.
+- Enforces Ethereum mainnet — prompts a network switch on the wrong chain.
+- Full transaction lifecycle: wallet confirmation → on-chain confirming →
+  confirmed, each with an Etherscan link. Errors (including user rejection)
+  are surfaced in plain language. Balances refresh on confirmation.
+
+## Running locally
+
+```bash
+npm install
+cp .env.example .env.local   # add a WalletConnect project id (and optional RPC)
+npm run dev                  # http://localhost:3000  → /pay
+```
+
+Environment variables (see `.env.example`):
+
+- `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID` — required for wallet connection; get
+  a free id at <https://cloud.reown.com>.
+- `NEXT_PUBLIC_MAINNET_RPC_URL` — optional dedicated RPC (Alchemy/Infura).
+  Recommended for production; falls back to a public RPC otherwise.
+
+## Scripts
+
+- `npm run dev` — dev server
+- `npm run build` / `npm start` — production build & serve
+- `npm run typecheck` — `tsc --noEmit`
+
+## Layout
+
+```
+src/
+  app/
+    layout.tsx        root layout + providers
+    providers.tsx     wagmi + RainbowKit + React Query
+    page.tsx          / → redirect to /pay
+    pay/page.tsx      the app: connect gate, balances, pay form
+    globals.css
+  components/
+    BalancesCard.tsx  USDC + ETH balances, no-gas warning
+    PayForm.tsx       recipient/amount inputs, validation, tx lifecycle
+  hooks/
+    useBalances.ts    USDC (balanceOf) + native ETH balance reads
+  lib/
+    usdc.ts           address, decimals, ABI
+    wagmi.ts          wagmi/RainbowKit config (mainnet)
+    amount.ts         safe human-amount → base-units parsing
+    format.ts         display helpers
+```
diff --git a/next.config.mjs b/next.config.mjs
